r1"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maechler</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Jornot</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wollheim</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Hydrogen peroxide alters mitochondrial activation and insulin secretion in pancreatic beta cells.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>274</volume><fpage>27905</fpage><lpage>27913</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10488138</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006500-Portha2"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Portha</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Movassat</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Cuzin-Tourrel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailbe</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Giroix</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>The neonatally streptozotocin-induced (n-STZ) rat model of Type 2 Diabetes. Several variants with multiple and complementary talents.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Shafrir</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>Animal models of Diabetes</source><publisher-name>Taylor and Francis</publisher-name><fpage>221</fpage><lpage>248</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006500-Jonas1"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jonas</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Guiot</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Rahier</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Henquin</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><a